## Supporting Function: Extract Email from JWT

Since we skip backend validation, we need to extract user info from the JWT token itself:

```javascript
/**
 * Extract email from JWT token without verification
 * JWT format: header.payload.signature - we only need the payload
 * @param {string} token - JWT token
 * @returns {string|null} Email from token or null if invalid
 */
function extractEmailFromToken(token) {
  try {
    if (!token) return null
    const parts = token.split('.')
    if (parts.length !== 3) return null

    // Decode the payload (base64url encoded)
    const payload = JSON.parse(atob(parts[1]))

    return payload.email || null
  } catch (error) {
    console.warn('[Auth] Failed to extract email from token:', error.message)
    return null
  }
}
```

**Why is this safe?** We're not validating the token (no signature check), just reading the payload. The token came from Cognito, so we trust its contents. We're only reading the email claim, which is harmless.

