## Complete Token Refresh Flow (Fixed)

Here's how the complete refresh flow now works:

```
1. User refreshes page
   ↓
2. App calls fetchSession() to restore session
   ↓
3. Check if token exists in localStorage
   ├─ NO → return null (not logged in)
   └─ YES → continue
   ↓
4. Try to validate current token with backend
   ├─ SUCCESS → return user session (stay logged in)
   └─ FAILED → continue to step 5
   ↓
5. Token expired, call refreshTokens()
   ├─ Build URL: API_BASE_URL + '/api/auth/refresh'
   ├─ Send native fetch() with refresh token
   ├─ Cognito validates refresh token and returns new tokens
   ├─ Store new tokens in localStorage
   └─ Return new tokens
   ↓
6. Extract email from JWT without backend validation
   ├─ Split token on '.'
   ├─ Decode base64url middle section
   ├─ Read 'email' from payload
   └─ Return user session with new tokens
   ↓
7. User stays logged in ✓
```

